#=GF CC This family represents the c-myc internal ribosome entry site (IRES). The
#=GF CC mammalian c-myc gene is a proto-oncogene which is required for cell
#=GF CC proliferation, transformation and death. c-myc mRNA has an alternative
#=GF CC method of translation via internal ribosome entry where ribosomes are
#=GF CC recruited to the IRES located in the 5' UTR thus bypassing the typical
#=GF CC eukaryotic cap-dependent translation pathway [1].
#=GF WK c-myc_internal_ribosome_entry_site_(IRES)
#=GF SQ 23

